<title>BRAZIL: Brazil 1996 trade gap was $5.541 bln -source.</title>
<headline>Brazil 1996 trade gap was $5.541 bln -source.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil posted a record trade deficit of $5.541 billion in 1996 after a gap of $3.157 billion the year before, a government source said.</p>
<p>The source, requesting anonymity, said December saw a trade gap of $1.787 billion.</p>
<p>The official trade figures were due to be announced at 1230 local/1430 GMT.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
